    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 3 • 1:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-pearl-girl/paragraph-3.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 3 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "At four fifty-eight, the Grants are drinking coffee near the museum. “Julia, do you have the guide book?” Mr. Grant asks. “No, Carl. You have it,” Mrs. Grant says. They look for the guidebook in their bags, then Mr. Grant says, “Oh no, I remember now. It’s on a chair near ’Girl with a Pearl Earring’. My passport is in that book!” Kate gets up quickly. “Stay here,” she says. “I can find it.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
