    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 12 • 9:04"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-pearl-girl/paragraph-12.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 12 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "At 9:15 that evening the bottle is a kilometer from the Black Dog. An old man is walking next to the canal. He stops. “A ship in a bottle!” he thinks. “That’s interesting.” He picks the bottle out of the water. Then he sees Kate’s note and reads it. “Thieves!” he thinks. “This is important.” He makes a call. “Hello? Police?” he says. He is talking very quickly. “Listen to this.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
